WHY AGPL, AND NOT SOMETHING MORE PERMISSIVE
-------------------------------------------
PyMuPDF is dual-licensed AGPL-3.0 / Artifex commercial, and this project links
it in two places: as the primary PDF text extractor, and as the foundation of
the vendored hidden-content detector, which reads per-span colour, size and
bounding boxes and renders pixmaps. AGPL is strong copyleft, so distributing
this work means the whole work is AGPL-3.0.

Removing that constraint means replacing PyMuPDF with pypdfium2 (BSD-3-Clause /
Apache-2.0) in BOTH places. The extractor swap is easy; rewriting the detector
is not, because it is vendored third-party code. Tracked as backlog item 18.

